  "root_cause_summary": "Production HOME's player universe was built from data/HOME_PLAYER_MASTER_TOP120.json (a generic K-Ranking TOP120 snapshot, gameCode-agnostic) via scripts/88's RANKING_DEFAULT fallback mode, NOT from KB's own official entry-list-based pipeline (2026090003_CURRENT_PLAYER_MASTER.json / 2026090003_PRE_PUBLIC_MASTER.json, both already exact-match verified against 2026090003_ENTRY_SNAPSHOT.json -- see KB_2026090003_FIELD_ARCHITECTURE_VERIFICATION_V1.json). scripts/88's own logic already correctly selects the entry-list-based TOURNAMENT_PRE mode whenever 2026090003_TIER2_PUBLICATION_GATE.json.overall_state == 'PASS' (confirmed PASS at audit time) -- the live production docs/ was simply never rebuilt+re-promoted since that gate started passing. This is a stale-build/stale-promotion defect, not a data-join defect.",
  "status": "SUPERSEDED_BY_V2",
  "supersession_reason": "This file compared HOME_RANKING_UNIVERSE (as rendered on production HOME at audit time) against OFFICIAL_ENTRY and treated the mismatch (including 황유민 being present) as a defect. OWNER DECISION corrected this premise: HOME and TOURNAMENT are two permanently separate populations that must never be compared this way -- HOME is never gameCode-scoped, so a \"home_only\"/\"official_only\" diff against it is not a meaningful defect signal. See KB_2026090003_FIELD_INTEGRITY_AUDIT_V2.json for the corrected audit (TOURNAMENT_FIELD vs OFFICIAL_ENTRY only) and KB_OWNER_DECISION_HOME_VS_TOURNAMENT_POPULATIONS_V1.json for the full decision record. Retained here, unedited otherwise, as an honest record of the investigation path this task actually took."
